# G-CL6 enforcement sentinel — read by deploy.sh cmd_check_doc_gates
# (--check-doc-gates --gate g-cl6, Stage 13 Phase A5) and by Check 28's deadline arm.
#
# First non-comment token decides whether a FINDINGS verdict BLOCKS:
#   warn     -> FINDINGS exits 2 and writes one warn-log row per failing artifact
#               under check "g-cl6" (advisory; Milestone close proceeds)
#   enforce  -> FINDINGS exits 1 and writes no row (blocking)
# Exit 0 belongs to CLEAN alone under either token, and N/A or NOT-EVALUATED exits 3
# under either token: this is an escalation dial, never a suppression dial.
#
# Ships `warn`. The flip to `enforce` is an OPERATOR DECISION after the shakedown the
# G-CL6 row of core/schemas/gate-criteria-spec.md declares, never auto-promoted by row
# count; record it in core/standards/gate-efficacy-standard.md § Flip-decision status.
# Until it is recorded, Check 28 reads GCL6_ROLLOUT_ARMED in core/deploy/deploy.sh and
# raises an issue once the escalation window passes.
warn
